From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:41:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 015/144] GreatDANE: fail closed and log in about:dane error
 trap; add fail-closed tests

- GreatDANEAbout: replace the silent catches (safeTarget, chain lookup,
  channel status, error-page URI) with console.error. A chain lookup error
  on a .pepe/.doge host now blocks (GD_NODE_NOT_READY) instead of letting
  the stock error page stand; an unreadable failure kind is treated as a
  TLSA/cert mismatch (GD_TLS_UNTRUSTED), never "site unreachable"; a
  rejected TLSA status query blocks as node-not-ready.
- Factor the decision into exported classifyChainFailure(); export
  _render() for tests; ErrorTrap.onLocationChange returns its promise.
- xpcshell test test_greatdane_failclosed.js (mock /gd/tlsa node): no TLSA
  record, TLSA/cert mismatch, node down / unanswerable, proxy filter never
  DIRECT, and no auto-continue/override on the interstitial.
